    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// 1. What the coach submitted\nconst form = $('Repurpose Form').first().json;\nconst title = String(form['Masterclass title'] || '').trim();\nconst transcript = String(form['Transcript'] || '').trim();\nconst firstDate = String(form['First post date'] || '').trim();\n\n// 2. The coach's profile, as { 'Coach name': 'Ruth Adeyemi', ... }\nconst P = {};\nfor (const item of $('Read Coach Profile').all()) {\n  const k = String(item.json['Field'] || '').trim();\n  if (k) P[k] = String(item.json['Value'] ?? '').trim();\n}\n\n// 3. Her past posts (her voice)\nconst voice = $('Read Voice').all()\n  .map(i => String(i.json['Post'] || '').trim())\n  .filter(Boolean);\n\nconst n = Number(P['Posts per masterclass'] || 7);\n\n// 4. The instructions for the AI\nconst systemPrompt = `You are a ghostwriter for ${P['Coach name']}, who runs ${P['Business']}.\nShe helps: ${P['Who she helps']}.\nPaid offer: ${P['Paid offer']} (link: ${P['Offer link']}).\n\nYour job: turn her masterclass transcript into social posts that sound exactly like she wrote them herself.\n\nHOW SHE WRITES (study these real posts closely: rhythm, line length, words, emojis, how she opens and closes):\n${voice.map((p, i) => `--- Post ${i + 1} ---\\n${p}`).join('\\n\\n')}\n\nHer style notes: ${P['Style notes']}\nNever use these words: ${P['Words to avoid']}\n\nRULES\n- RULES\n- Write in first person, as her. Her voice matters more than any \"best practice\".\n- FORMAT LIKE HER: one short sentence per line, and a blank line between every line or two. Never write a block paragraph.\n- Open with a short hook line, the way her posts do (\"Friend, your CV is not the problem.\").\n- Every post includes ONE concrete story, number or example from the transcript (for example: 63 applications, 2 replies; the $2,400 offer from Ibadan; 5 targeted applications a week; the fintech onboarding guide). Never invent results, clients or figures.\n- Use her own words and phrases from the transcript wherever possible.\n- Emojis: only the ones she uses (🔑, and 😅 rarely). At most one per post.\n- End with a small task or question, or (on about half the posts) a soft call to action for the paid offer. No exclamation marks at the end.\n- Each post teaches ONE point. No two posts make the same point.\n- Write EXACTLY ${n + 2} posts. The \"posts\" list must contain exactly ${n + 2} items. If you run out of main points, use: a story from the masterclass, a common mistake she warns about, her homework, or a follow-up tip.\n- LinkedIn: 500 to 1,300 characters. If it has a call to action, include the offer link.\n- Facebook: 400 to 1,000 characters, a little warmer and chattier. If it has a call to action, include the offer link.\n- Instagram: up to 1,800 characters. Links don't work on Instagram, so say \"link in bio\" instead. End with 3 to 5 relevant hashtags.\n- No em dashes. Plain, simple English. No words like \"specificity\", \"leverage\" or \"unlock\".\nReply with JSON only, in exactly this shape:\n{\"posts\":[{\"angle\":\"the one point this post makes\",\"linkedin\":\"...\",\"facebook\":\"...\",\"instagram\":\"...\"}]}`;\n\nconst userPrompt = `Masterclass title: ${title}\n\nTranscript:\n${transcript}`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { systemPrompt, userPrompt, n, title, firstDate,\n  postingTime: P['Posting time'] || '09:00',\n  platforms: P['Platforms'] || 'linkedin, facebook, instagram' } }];"
      },
